<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka T-bill yields fall at auction.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka T-bill yields fall at auction.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lankan treasury bill yields continued to decline, with weighted average of three, six and 12-month bills falling by 1.12 percentage points, 0.47 and 0.02 respectively, at Wednesday's auction, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>		  bids received   bids accepted   avg yield</p>
<p>    3 months     4,313	     1,562	  12.86 (13.98)</p>
<p>    6 months     2,446	     1,206	  14.53 (15.00)</p>
<p>    12 months    1,077		 308	  15.28 (15.30)</p>
<p>NOTE - Bids in million rupees, yields in percent (previous week's yields in brackets).</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
